# chat: JEVCODE_MOCK_INTAKE=ambiguous — `the date parsing` is answered like any other message and Jev's unsure reading
# only adds the `do it` offer to the reply. No card is drawn, the composer is never blocked ("waiting for y/n" must
# never appear) and no run starts: the next message decides that (chat-ambiguous-y sends `do it`).
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send the date parsing
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* 
expect make that a task
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
